  "reasoning": "The pipeline correctly builds fold-based target-encoding maps from training rows only, uses OOF encoding for final model training, and applies saved full-fit maps at prediction without refitting, so validation labels never leak into training. The blend search uses honest OOF probabilities on val folds, and predictions output row_id/prediction in original label space with preserved row order. I found no P0 data leakage or P1 critical bugs; minor concerns like OOF-vs-full-fit TE distribution shift and edge-case blend weight fallback are suboptimal but not correctness bugs."
